{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1538209-i-did-a-thing-hunter-and-construct-linages","id":1538209,"title":"I did a thing - Hunter and Construct Linages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-07T13:26:13-07:00","id":1538209,"title":"I did a thing - Hunter and Construct Linages","content":"<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Helsings (inspired by core mortals, hunters, bits of demon the descent)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Curse is a disease and we are\u2026 no, we\u2019re not the cure. That\u2019s like saying that we\u2019re here to kill off the Curse. We\u2019re not \u2013 after all, we\u2019re cursed too. Can\u2019t deal with Curse without getting some on yourself too. Except, instead of being turned into something that defies the laws of reality as we know it? The curse inverts instead and we become more real, more human than ever, so much that it bleeds back over to the other side again. And, yeah, we can turn that against anything that isn\u2019t native to our world. Just don\u2019t forget that we get just as many angels as we do devils from it all.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Skills - Empathy, Ranged Combat, Technology</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Practical Training \u2013 </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bleed 1 curse die. You gain a +1 Enhancement on all rolls that use your Role skills (as modified by any spells or edges) for the scene. Gain a minor complication on all Actions using skills that are not part of any of your Paths.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Only Human - </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You can spend 1 Momentum to negate the side effects from any Wicked Success or Cruel Failure. Alternatively, spend 1 Momentum to no longer register as Accursed to any supernatural senses* - this may provoke a Clash against some spells or abilities. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>MAJOR INHERITANCE - </i></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your Lineage Path skills count as part of your Role Path skills for all mechanics, including character creation. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You may establish a fact within a scene once per session, as if you had spent a Momentum, without cost. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* Note - Accursed have a kind of innate, passive ability to sense when someone is another Accursed, and possibly can detect other kinds of supernatural beings/effects.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Torment: NIMBY -</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Other supernatural beings hanging around? Not in your backyard! A character with this torment strains against the desire to remove the prickling sensation of supernatural forces from around them. When they succumb, they must somehow remove the source of the supernatural from their immediate presence in some manner. (Helsings using Only Human do not provoke this reaction). </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Torment: Zealous - </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The world is a large, scary place. And that\u2019s before we start adding in the Accursed, Outsiders, Liminal spaces, and more. Its no wonder that many people turn to religions or other authorities for answers and comfort. A character with this torment has found one such source of answers that works for them, and often feels the need to share the Good News with others. When they succumbs, they spend time demonstrating or extolling their beliefs to any and all present, preferably loudly so that everyone can hear or see. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Damnation - </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When a Helsing hits 0 Curse Die, they end up falling into their Role, far more strongly than ever, to the point of obsession, regardless of any moral compass. Any attempt to take actions unrelated to the Role skills suffer a medium complication on every roll. If the complication is not bought off, then the character must perform an action using one of the Role skills instead. With the wrong Role, this might turn a character into a killer.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Damnation Resolution - </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Helsing needs to remember there\u2019s more to life outside of their enforced obsession. The character must somehow add two Momentum to the pool, then spend said Momentum to generate enough hits to overcome the Complication on a non-Role skill. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Practices</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> \u2013 Exorcism (based on VtM\u2019s True Faith, CofD\u2019s Abjuration, Benedictions, Castigation); The Professional (Professional Training on crack, bits of DtD\u2019s Cover / Legend system, Group Tactics); Arsenal (relics, elixirs, and sufficiently advanced technology). </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Families- like above, each family's major inheritance will include key skills added to the &quot;Role Path&quot; skills, which in turn will be affected by the Professional Practice's spells as well as the Practical Training buffs. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Slayers - Buffy, anyone? The Chosen One by any other name. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Demon Hunter Bloodline - Halfway between an anime ninja clan and the Winchester Brothers. More sneaky than direct combat. Use talismans?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Totally Renamed SCP Foundation - United Nation-based group that specializes in isolating hazardous items and \u201cbeings\u201d</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exorcist - priest-like people, be they christian style or otherwise.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Watchers - observe and record, but never interfere? Overlap with Network Zero?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shadow Market - underworld figures that leverage supernatural connections to gather political influence and wealth (the mobster from Dresden Files?) Mercinaries. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Hunt Club - actively seeks out supernatural challenges and battlegrounds for the thrill of overcoming them. Touches into Slasher territory. Antagonist vibes? Anyone can join. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lineage-only Edges</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supernatural Tolerance - Gain a +1 enhancement to any defensive roll against a supernatural power. This does not include Clashes. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Group Tactics - You may use the highest rated of your Bonds present in the scene for any teamwork roll, even if the teamwork roll doesn\u2019t include said Bond\u2019s target. One person you have a bond with can benefit from your bond rating even if you are not taking part in the teamwork roll. </span></span><br /> <br /> Note - When I sat down to do this, I wanted a few things. Above all else, I wanted to avoid pulling fantasy racism into the mix, and I really, really liked the idea of Professional Training being what made Hunters really click. Professional Training has now become the Role path, so I tried to devise the Helsings as being based around interacting with the Role Path.<br /> <br /> This Lineage was primarily inspired by Hunter the Vigil, Supernatural, Buffy the Vampire Slayer, the anime Helsing, SCP Foundation stories, bits of Dresden Files.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":"old name references removed), moved second lineage down 07-08-2024, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T13:26:47-07:00","id":1538210,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Constructs</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Constructs. The created ones. Golems, gargoyles, zombies and risen skeletons, living dolls, androids, homoculi, robots and more. Perhaps you are a new being that just came to life, or perhaps you were human but now have a bit of an upgrade. Who made you what you are tonight? Sometimes, it\u2019s another member of the same family, looking for a companion. Or perhaps it was one of the Hungry, or a Sorcerer, or any one of the other Accursed. Maybe it was even a regular mortal or an Outsider or something even stranger. All that matters is that it's your life, and it's now or never. </i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skills - Enigmas, Esoterica, Artistry OR Enigmas, Science, Technology OR Enigmas, Medicine, Survival</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Analytical Mind - Bleed 1 curse die to gain +1 enhancement to all mental rolls. Influence actions not based on logic also have their difficulty raised by 1; this applies both when the Constructed is doing the Influencing or when someone is trying to Influence them. </i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Purity of the Machine - </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Human bodies are failable. They require a delicate balance just to live, let alone survive injuries. The Constructed bodies, in many ways, are far more robust and simple, even those made from wood or flesh instead of stone or metal. Treat the Constructed as if they had Armor equal to their Entanglement. Further, Constructed have no need to eat, drink or sleep, as they\u2019re powered directly by their Curse. Toxins that affect humans may not work on the Constructed either.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ship of Theseus - </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As constructed beings, members of this Lineage cannot heal on their own over time without a spell or other power. Instead, they must rebuild themselves using the same materials they were made from, determined by the chosen Lineage Path skills. Artistry and Esoterica implies specially carved wood, stone or clay parts; Medicine and Survival uses biological parts, akin to the famed Frankenstein Monster; and Science and Technology imply machine parts. Whenever you or someone on your behalf makes a healing roll, they may replace Medicine with either of the aforementioned Lineage Path skills. You are not limited to one healing action per scene, and failure to buy off a complication from combat-relevant status effects does cause them to worsen or gain a new status effect. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In theory, this could allow a Construct to live forever by avoiding wear and tear and replacing worn out parts. Reality is rarely so kind, especially for those who rely on human brains to function. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>MAJOR INHERITANCE - </i></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Perfected Body - So long as you\u2019re holding 2 Curse dice, Actions involving the Physical Arena benefit from the 9-again rule. Once per scene, so long as you\u2019re holding 2 Curse dice, you may choose to bleed 1 curse die to reroll all dice not showing a hit on a failed action involving the Physical Arena. </i></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Torment: Dysphoria - neither your body nor your mind is your own, but one shaped by another for their designs. When the character succumbs to this torment, they engage in acts of self-destruction, ignoring their own health and wellbeing as they fall into depression and engage in rote, mindless actions instead of speaking up for themselves, or coming across as cold and unfeeling.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Torment: Abandonment - The Constructed\u2019s relationship with their maker isn\u2019t the best, and often (or entirely) left to their own devices for long stretches of time. When the Constructed succumbs, it pushes them to act out, either by picking fights or engaging in other intimate activities with others, regardless of the consequences. </i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Damnation - </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When a Constructed reaches 0 curse dice, they run out of energy to power their bodies. They have a number of turns equal to their Entanglement (including the turn the character bled their last Curse die) before they shut down and gain the Taken Out (unconscious?) Condition. This Condition does not Resolve at the end of combat like normal, but will if taken to a Place of Deferment. Upon gaining the Taken Out condition, the character loses all memories of the last scene - short term memory loss, not saving to disk, etc. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Damnation Resolution</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - The Taken Out Condition must be Resolved via first aid action, using the same rules under </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ship of Theseus, </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">or taken to a Place of Deferment</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>.</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Depending on the individual Constructed physiology, this may be as simple as plugging a robot into a wall socket to recharge or as involved as restarting a fusion reactor or something more exotic, like a specialized serum injection. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Practices</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Electricity (lightning elementalism, control over electronic devices and minor control over human nervous system), Forge (the fires of creation and inspiration, radiation and light), Metamorphosis (control over the body\u2019s shape and abilities, chimera- or transformer-like abilities, building towards your ideal body goals)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Families - Each of the families are defined by PURPOSE, the reason that they\u2019re made. A robot built for labor is considered part of the same Family as the Golem of Prauge as well as the skeleton servant raised by a necromancer, each just made with different materials.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gargoyle - those built to watch and guard</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Doll / Android - those built to be a pretty companion</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Golem / Robot - those built to labor and slave (Mars Rover restored and turned into one?)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effigy - those built to be sacrificed. Alternatively, those actually sacrificed but brought back wrong. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Homunculi / zombie / Frankenstein - those who\u2019s making was their Purpose, but now are without.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cyborg - augmented humans rebuilt to be Faster, Stronger, Better</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lineage-only Edges</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weatherproof - you\u2019ve been proofed against extreme environments, and don\u2019t suffer from them like others would. This includes a number of exotic environments found Outside or in Liminal Spaces.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Residual Memories - Whether it's from another\u2019s brain, or the information used to build an AI, your mind has a number of memories floating around that can be tapped into at need. Choose a number of skills equal to the cost of this Edge (1 to 3). You may spend a Momentum to allocate a number of dots equal to your Entanglement to those skills for a scene. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T13:27:18-07:00","id":1538211,"title":"","content":"Enjoy everyone. Hope it inspires your games or otherwise gives you ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-07-2024, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T14:38:54-07:00","id":1538214,"title":"","content":"That is superbly good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}